Explanation:

1. We hook into the existing `render()` loop, immediately after appending the passed‐audits clump.
2. We walk through each `auditRef` in that clump, collect all their `warnings` arrays, and flatten them.
3. If any warnings exist, we create a new `<div class="lh-warnings">` block, prepend the `"Warnings:"` heading (from your UI strings), then build a `<ul>` of `<li>` items.
4. Finally, we append that block into the category container right after the passed audits, so the existing test will find a single `.lh-warnings` element with the expected text.
